WEBVTT

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:06.000
Nice body you got there. I'm jealous.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:12.670
Well, it's been about 40 days since I
enrolled here, but I'm no spring chicken.

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:16.090
But, I still do it for my health.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:27.520
I'm Jonathan Earp, as in "Wyatt Earp."

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:29.770
A tough name for someone who don't look it.

00:01:31.730 --> 00:01:34.280
You're Duke Togo, right?

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:40.160
W-What? Your name's on the register.

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:40.910
Glad to meet.

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:51.630
I still say I envy that body of yours.

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:55.840
By the way, why don't we grab some dinner?

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:58.890
I know a place that really hits the spot.

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:01.220
Uh... oh, and...

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:04.970
And I know of this really swinging place too.

00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:12.900
I walk unsteadily on paths to nowhere

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:17.030
wondering what I should do right now.

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:23.490
I play the song you like on the car stereo

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:28.040
with the volume up and my feelings crystallized

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:33.670
driving on streets with no crossroads or signals

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:39.090
with a speed that will catch up with you.

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:43.550
So faraway - let's run!

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:49.850
And let's not bother with the breaks - full throttle.

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:54.150
Oh someday - one of these days

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:59.240
You'll be at my place where nobody can find you.

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:05.330
Whenever you suffer a breakdown one can't see

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:10.920
depend on me for your repairs.

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:15.290
So faraway - let's run!

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:21.510
We'll reset and start again - even at our limit.

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:25.810
Oh someday - one of these days

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:31.850
If I'm with you we'll find our dream.

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:42.700
Murderous Crosspoints

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:49.660
You stupid or something, babe?

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:50.410
You serious?

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:51.790
Let's go!

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:09.180
Here's to that magnificent body of yours.

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:12.310
So are you having a good time?

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:14.690
I'll hear you out.

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:19.480
The reason why we're here, Wyatt Earp.

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:22.990
H-Hey, no need to call me that...

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:27.990
R-Right you are. Okay then...

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:31.450
That's $50,000.

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:34.960
If you listen to my request, it's all yours.

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:38.500
How about it? Not a bad deal, is it?

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:40.090
Also...

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:46.970
These are the detailed notes I took of
your strength training for the past week.

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:51.640
You are truly very well built.

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:57.020
But what I was really interested in was how you worked your arms.

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:01.570
Like the muscles that turn your hands up or down.

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:10.910
You turn your palms forward and inwards then
outwards and back in a continual rotating exercise.

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:17.710
Doing that exercise makes shooting a gun easy.

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:19.420
I'll bet.

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:21.750
Get to the point.

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:26.720
I just want you to pull the trigger.

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:29.180
So there's your $50,000. How about it?

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:31.350
So I'm going to eat a murder?

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:32.720
Shh!

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:35.560
Don't put is so crudely.

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:39.650
All you got to do is move your
finger, plus you won't get caught.

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:40.860
I guarantee it.

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:43.990
All the preparations have been made.

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:46.860
All you need to do is pull the trigger.

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:48.660
Please.

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:52.410
I really need to make this happen.

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:35.870
I wasn't late, I wanted make sure
that you really did come here early.

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:42.040
So Jonathan Earp is dead serious about that?

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:44.210
He watched me exercise my hands.

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:46.260
Very good.

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:49.970
That means Jonathan Earp will fully carry out his plan.

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:53.390
His plan to assassinate Brown.

00:06:56.020 --> 00:07:01.060
I've transferred the $3 million compensation to your Swiss bank account.

00:07:01.060 --> 00:07:05.440
I wish you the best of luck, Mr. Golgo 13.

00:07:23.170 --> 00:07:29.090
This is just one of our recreational facilities we manage at ABC Leisure Concern.

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:33.050
Bowling's been regaining popularity lately.

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:40.560
We're a large-scale leisure enterprise based in Chicago that manages everything from movie theaters to casinos.

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:48.650
All right! Lucky!

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:19.020
Go for it, Ann!

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:30.440
You're always in perfect form, Ann.

00:08:33.650 --> 00:08:34.910
H-Him!

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:39.660
Papa, you're late! You made me wait an hour!

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:41.200
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:47.880
H-Hey, we got company here, can you quit that?

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:51.630
I used to be a pro bowler.

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:54.880
Now I handle the Chicago branch.

00:08:56.840 --> 00:08:59.510
This is how I start off each workday.

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:04.020
I'll be in a good mood the entire day if I get a strike.

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:08.190
Care to go a frame?

00:09:08.730 --> 00:09:09.270
No.

00:09:20.030 --> 00:09:22.080
Looks like I lost my rhythm today.

00:09:28.330 --> 00:09:31.050
Is that boob slacking off on the maintenance again?

00:09:31.590 --> 00:09:33.170
Get him out here!

00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:34.050
Y-Yes sir!

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:41.890
Papa, you promised to take me to a club today, right?

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:45.310
Uh, I'm afraid something's come up today.

00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:46.560
Why don't you go by yourself?

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:49.480
It's sucks going by myself!

00:09:50.860 --> 00:09:52.570
Say, wanna date?

00:09:52.570 --> 00:09:54.360
A-Are you stupid?

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:57.780
He and I are suppose to discuss something very important!

00:09:57.780 --> 00:10:00.490
Fine, I'll just find someone else to have a fling with.

00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:01.620
Let's go, guys!

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:03.080
A-Ann...

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:08.000
Come on, move it already!

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:10.130
Dammit, you all are so shiftless!

00:10:16.840 --> 00:10:18.380
You shithead!

00:10:19.930 --> 00:10:23.680
Chuck, do you always keep a
thumb up your ass or something?

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:27.390
Your next fuck-up's gonna cost ten percent of your pay, you hear?

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:30.940
But my pay has already been slashed drastically.

00:10:30.940 --> 00:10:32.770
It's your own damned fault!

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:36.400
And don't forget your manners either!

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:38.490
Are we clear?

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:41.620
Take him away!

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:49.120
Christ, a real shit-for-brains, that one.

00:10:59.430 --> 00:11:01.140
Go right ahead, further back.

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:07.980
What's going on?

00:11:09.890 --> 00:11:11.230
Have a seat.

00:11:12.900 --> 00:11:14.150
Don't mind me.

00:11:14.520 --> 00:11:16.230
I'll listen while standing.

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:19.070
O-Oh, is that right?

00:11:19.070 --> 00:11:22.070
Very well, I'll tell you about my plan.

00:11:22.490 --> 00:11:27.240
This room is both soundproof and bulletproof. We keep it around for private conversations.

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:31.670
And we're sitting under the man's portrait.

00:11:31.670 --> 00:11:33.920
Pretty ironic, don't you think?

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:42.890
Brown, our company president, will take off from an
airfield heading for his home in Canada at exactly 5PM.

00:11:43.840 --> 00:11:47.390
Just like he does every day like clockwork.

00:11:48.680 --> 00:11:56.980
We will head him off by taking off from a different
airfield at 5:15 and wait for him over Lake Michigan.

00:11:57.780 --> 00:12:00.240
He's not going to get away.

00:12:00.740 --> 00:12:05.990
The gun you'll be using has nocturnal vision, so you'll be covered even if it gets dark.

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:08.700
So he's definitely coming alone?

00:12:08.700 --> 00:12:10.700
He's that big of a piloting nut!

00:12:11.500 --> 00:12:16.000
Once the job's done, I'll go and get rid of Exhibit A, aka the plane.

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:19.420
The sea?

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:21.010
I can't tell you that!

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:23.510
For both our sakes.

00:12:24.390 --> 00:12:26.390
But I will tell you this much.

00:12:30.680 --> 00:12:35.770
Once I become the president, I'll attain an existence even you can't reach.

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:42.740
Still, I am more than willing to keep your future in mind.

00:12:44.030 --> 00:12:46.780
So let's go and scratch each other's backs.

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:52.080
Hmm?

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:08.300
Yeah, it's me. I'm about to go, so load my ball in the car.

00:13:08.930 --> 00:13:10.560
You've cleaned it, right?

00:13:11.430 --> 00:13:12.180
Good.

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:19.400
That ball's my lucky charm. Whenever I ride with that baby, I feel at ease.

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:54.640
You prick.

00:13:55.310 --> 00:13:56.310
You prick.

00:13:56.730 --> 00:13:59.360
Just you wait... just you wait!

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:24.340
That fool.

00:14:24.710 --> 00:14:26.220
What a dumbass.

00:15:15.970 --> 00:15:19.350
Looks like this watch has run out its lifespan.

00:15:19.350 --> 00:15:22.980
I got no choice but to keep replacing 'em.

00:16:10.070 --> 00:16:12.860
You sure know your way around a gun.

00:16:12.860 --> 00:16:18.870
You can probably tell by looking, but that's a Tanner with armor-piercing bullets.

00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:20.870
It didn't come cheap.

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:27.880
So you get to thinking about the biggest
reasons why a criminal act gets revealed.

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:34.180
Well, one would be the presence of witnesses, and the other is physical evidence.

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:38.260
However, there will be neither of those.

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:41.180
There are no witnesses in the wild blue yonder.

00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:46.650
And once I get rid of the gun and the plane
there will be no remaining physical evidence.

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:52.900
So what do you think? A perfect crime, right?

00:16:54.070 --> 00:16:59.450
The name "ABC Leisure Concern" includes the initials of three people, correct?

00:17:00.240 --> 00:17:01.330
That's right.

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:08.210
Creighton died in an auto accident, Brown's about to die, and the last one left is our chairman, Alba.

00:17:08.630 --> 00:17:11.760
That man is my backer.

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:14.220
So where did you hear that?

00:17:16.180 --> 00:17:17.220
He's here.

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:47.670
Damn turbulence!

00:18:11.020 --> 00:18:11.860
Left!

00:18:40.720 --> 00:18:42.680
Y... You did it.

00:18:42.680 --> 00:18:44.220
You did it!

00:18:49.600 --> 00:18:51.440
You did it! You killed him!

00:18:54.270 --> 00:18:58.280
All right, all that's left is to go and drop you off.

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:44.700
There now.

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:47.200
You can get off here.

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:51.460
I'll take you to the car that's parked by the hangar.

00:19:52.290 --> 00:19:54.080
Aren't you flying soon?

00:19:54.710 --> 00:19:57.710
I don't want to part with this for a second.

00:19:57.710 --> 00:19:59.550
Not one second.

00:20:28.490 --> 00:20:30.040
Chairman Alba!

00:20:31.710 --> 00:20:33.040
H... How?

00:20:35.880 --> 00:20:37.590
Right on time.

00:20:44.220 --> 00:20:45.220
Earp...

00:20:45.220 --> 00:20:48.430
You've really stepped in it this time.

00:20:53.310 --> 00:20:54.310
H-Hey!

00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:57.940
I never thought that you would go and kill Brown.

00:21:00.400 --> 00:21:05.950
When I said I'd become your backer, that
was not a green light to go and kill Brown!

00:21:08.330 --> 00:21:09.450
That son of a...!

00:21:14.710 --> 00:21:19.960
Now that I know about this, you're no longer just my subordinate.

00:21:20.380 --> 00:21:24.470
You'll be serving me hand and foot for life, Jonathan Earp!

00:21:55.330 --> 00:21:57.330
Yahoo!

00:21:57.330 --> 00:21:59.670
I gotcha, you gaping asshole!

00:21:59.670 --> 00:22:03.460
This is for all the times you've
treated me like shit! Suck on that!

00:22:03.460 --> 00:22:05.970
What now? What now? What-!

00:22:40.830 --> 00:22:45.960
I enjoyed the little things.

00:22:48.010 --> 00:22:53.180
I loved when you gave me a flower every day

00:22:53.930 --> 00:22:59.270
instead of just one big bouquet

00:22:59.980 --> 00:23:04.110
of flowers.

00:23:06.190 --> 00:23:11.740
It was like a romance novel.

00:23:12.370 --> 00:23:16.330
Surely someday... just kidding.

00:23:16.660 --> 00:23:19.710
I had a dream.

00:23:20.080 --> 00:23:25.420
Your face shined eternally.

00:23:26.250 --> 00:23:32.010
Because I think of you all the time.

00:23:32.430 --> 00:23:37.560
I'm sorry, but on a lonely night like this

00:23:38.520 --> 00:23:44.060
I'm remembering you, but

00:23:44.360 --> 00:23:48.650
I won't cry like I did that day.

00:23:50.400 --> 00:23:51.820
I won't.

00:24:02.870 --> 00:24:12.180
A wine tasting was about to commence at a French manor

00:24:13.180 --> 00:24:20.810
while Golgo looked down from a hill holding his M16.

00:24:21.270 --> 00:24:24.900
Next time on Golgo 13: Proud Wine.

00:24:22.350 --> 00:24:27.480
Proud Wine

00:24:25.610 --> 00:24:30.110
Don't stand behind him, if you value your life.
